tooling, the test vectors, and the reference implementation.

See LICENSE for the full text.

That earlier grant is not withdrawn, and could not be: CC-BY-4.0 section
2(a)(1) grants a perpetual, irrevocable license. Anyone who received this
specification under CC-BY-4.0 keeps it under CC-BY-4.0, for that copy,
forever. What changes is the offer made to everyone from here on. A
specification whose subject is that agreements bind the party that signed
them does not get to make an exception for its own license.

Rationale for the change: one license across the specification, the
conformance suite and the reference implementation removes the question of
which grant covers a file that is partly prose and partly a generated
artifact — the vectors are both. Apache-2.0's explicit patent grant is the
reason to prefer it over CC-BY-4.0 for a protocol whose normative text and
its executable half are the same deliverable.

